How to Run the PowerShell Service Account Ownership Script
Step 1: Save the PowerShell Script
Open Notepad or Visual Studio Code, paste the PowerShell script, and save it as:
C:\Scripts\ServiceAccountOwnership.ps1
Make sure the file extension is .ps1 and not .txt.
Step 2: Create Required Folders
Open PowerShell and run:
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path C:\Scripts -Force
New-Item -ItemType Directory -Path C:\Reports -Force
Step 3: Place the Input Excel File
Copy the Excel report into the following location and ensure the name matches the script configuration:
C:\Reports\AD-ServiceAccountFile.xlsx
Step 4: Install the ImportExcel Module
Open PowerShell and run:
Install-Module ImportExcel -Scope CurrentUser
If prompted to install the NuGet provider or trust PSGallery, enter Y.
Verify the module installation:
Get-Module ImportExcel -ListAvailable
Step 5: Check the Active Directory Module
The script uses Get-ADUser to resolve manager information. Check whether the Active Directory PowerShell module is available:
Get-Module ActiveDirectory -ListAvailable
If available, test importing it:
Import-Module ActiveDirectory
If the module is not installed, RSAT/Active Directory PowerShell tools may need to be installed by your IT administrator.
Step 6: Check Script Execution Policy
Run:
Get-ExecutionPolicy
If scripts are blocked, use the following command. This applies only to the current PowerShell window:
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
Step 7: Run the Script
Navigate to the script folder:
cd C:\Scripts
Run the script:
.\ServiceAccountOwnership.ps1
Alternative command:
powershell.exe -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File "C:\Scripts\ServiceAccountOwnership.ps1"
Step 8: Run in Test Mode First
Before enabling production email notifications, ensure the script contains:
$TestMode = $true
In test mode, the script processes the accounts and generates results but does not send actual emails.
Step 9: Check the Output
After successful execution, check:
C:\Reports\AD-ServiceAccountFile_Result.xlsx
C:\Reports\AD-ServiceAccountFile_Log.txt
Common Errors
Error: Running scripts is disabled
Run:
Set-ExecutionPolicy -Scope Process -ExecutionPolicy Bypass
Error: Import-Excel is not recognized
Run:
Install-Module ImportExcel -Scope CurrentUser -Force
Recommended Testing Order
1.	Keep $TestMode = $true.
2.	Confirm the Excel file path is correct.
3.	Confirm the ImportExcel module is installed.
4.	Confirm the Active Directory module is available.
5.	Run the script.
6.	Review the output Excel file and log file.
7.	Validate the Manager and ManagedBy results.
8.	Only after validation, configure SMTP and change $TestMode = $false.
Important Production Note
Do not enable real email sending until the Manager-to-email lookup is validated. If the Manager column contains only display names, a display-name lookup can return the wrong person when duplicate names exist.
